{:edb/db-before-t 1209 :edb/db-after-t 1210 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534522 50 #inst "2026-10-12T01:49:27.327Z" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186133726 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424144 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186133726 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424145 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186133728 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424143 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186133729 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424146 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186133729 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424147 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186419941 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424137 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186419941 1078 #edb/ref 17592186419896 13194139534522 17592186045417 false] [17592186419941 1078 #edb/ref 17592186424137 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186419955 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{108}x(x+2),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186419955 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{108}x(x+2),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." 13194139534522 17592186045417 false] [17592186419955 1074 "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $0\\le x\\le 6,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 1, & x>6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{108}t(t+2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={\\frac{1}{324}{t}^{2}(t+3)|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{324}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{108}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{3}}{324}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{108}, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 1, & x>6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186419955 1074 "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $0\\le x\\le 6,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 1, & x>6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{108}t(t+2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={\\frac{1}{324}{t}^{2}(t+3)|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{324}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{108}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{3}}{324}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{108}, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 1, & x>6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534522 17592186045417 false] [17592186424116 1080 "\\frac{5}{32}" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424116 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424116 1083 #uuid "08f9e3f9-5178-5f25-af6a-daa6ab351cf7" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424117 1080 "\\frac{25}{32}" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424117 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424117 1083 #uuid "0fbef09a-e8ff-5508-9488-c6c964ed4029" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424118 1080 "\\frac{5}{16}" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [1759218642