2186424142 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424120 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424142 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424124 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424142 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424142 1077 "selection" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424142 1078 #edb/ref 17592186424117 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424142 1079 #uuid "e8a9fa39-360a-5d80-8fca-fb43fa89be61" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424143 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424140 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424143 1069 "q-89659" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424143 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424143 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}(x-2),\\, & 3\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<3 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 3\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424143 1072 #uuid "4087990a-4ed6-57e2-a3df-7711bffc8cc9" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424143 1074 "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $3\\le x\\le 4,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<3 \\\\ {\\int }_{3}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 3\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{3}^{x}\\frac{2}{3}(t-2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={\\frac{1}{3}t(t-4)|}_{3}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}x(x-4)+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-4x+3}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<3 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}-4x+3}{3}, & 3\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424144 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424138 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424144 1069 "q-210757" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424144 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424144 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{{x}^{5}},\\, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0,\\, & x<1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424144 1072 #uuid "481bd08b-bf47-54b5-b36c-cbccf6d7d5b3" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424144 1074 "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $x\\ge 1,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}\\frac{4}{{t}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={-\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}|}_{1}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1, \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424145 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424141 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424145 1069 "q-126151" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424145 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424145 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{20}{e}^{-x/20},\\, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424145 1072 #uuid "9bc932a7-b704-59fd-b0c1-c79e29ca1ef0" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424145 1074 "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $x\\ge 0,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{20}{e}^{-t/20}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & =-{e}^{-t/20}{|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x/20}+1 \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-x/20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0, \\\\ 1-{e}^{-x/20}, & x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424146 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424139 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424146 1069 "q-89738" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424146 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424146 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ 1-{e}^{-2x}, & x\\ge 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(X>2).$" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424146 1072 #uuid "a285feed-066b-52a2-a5c2-8c1c741cc3d0" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424146 1074 "We can perform this computation using the complement, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>2) & =1-P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =1-F(2) \\\\  & =1-(1-{e}^{-4}) \\\\  & ={e}^{-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424147 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424142 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424147 1069 "q-126178" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424147 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424147 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{96}({x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}-3), & 1\\le x\\le 3 \\\\ 1, & x>3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(X>2).$" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424147 1072 #uuid "cbafb4bb-6bd6-540c-9367-06ab0b677b70" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true] [17592186424147 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nHence, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>2) & =1-P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =1-F(2) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{96}({2}^{4}+2(2)^{2}-3) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{21}{96} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{32}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534522 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-08f9e3f9-5178-5f25-af6a-daa6ab351cf7" 17592186424116 "answer-0fbef09a-e8ff-5508-9488-c6c964ed4029" 17592186424117 "answer-17a75073-455d-5976-ba1c-b3f22347a040" 17592186424118 "answer-2ea5a4d8-cee6-5f5b-9559-0597059ae4e9" 17592186424119 "answer-3111cc62-9d7f-5a21-8f89-33bb0b009b9c" 17592186424120 "answer-36a08189-b91b-5a20-b7ab-cd5b33daebf3" 17592186424121 "answer-47fbec0e-7c87-50b2-b20a-31977a9c56d7" 17592186424122 "answer-4e656111-b56c-58e0-b523-b0edd9650549" 17592186424123 "answer-529bbff1-ee9c-5239-b9f3-b7e4f26f33fe" 17592186424124 "answer-616c4e05-5002-58ab-b3bb-58e10d3a8092" 17592186424125 "answer-624998d8-03eb-57ee-930b-8fdefbbf7c6a" 17592186424126 "answer-63f468a1-66c1-59cb-86ef-0e77953938a7" 17592186424127 "answer-6f86bba4-cf32-5b63-95b2-322fa3b1a857" 17592186424128 "answer-713d0b3e-c9bb-554a-b337-a9f036666fa2" 17592186424129 "answer-74a5f07c-c3bf-5c2c-a586-05b1a17ea2f2" 17592186424130 "answer-7b06527d-a247-549f-874c-21500